From: Bryan Roscoe <bryanroscoe@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:41:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] AI: classify named counters by the placing card's statics
 (Omo's everything counter)

A generic counter such as Omo, Queen of Vesuva's everything counter has no
rules meaning of its own; the static that cares about it ("each land with an
everything counter on it is every land type") says what it does.
counter_sign_polarity saw only the name and returned Contextual, so target
selection fell back to "assume harmful" and aimed the counter at opponents'
permanents. In the Yama deck lab (157 replayed four-player games) the Easy AI
put 873 of 886 everything counters on opponents' lands and creatures.

counter_polarity_for_source reads the polarity off the placing object's own
statics whose affected filter requires at least one counter of that kind
(CR 122.1 + CR 613.1): unanimous beneficial or harmful modes/modifications
decide, anything else stays Contextual. effect_polarity_for_source applies it
to PutCounter, PutCounterAll and RemoveCounter (inverted) and is used where
the source is known: is_spell_beneficial, player_impact (targeted object and
player impact) and anti_self_harm's slot_polarity. modification_polarity now
also counts AddAllLandTypes and AddAllBasicLandTypes ("in addition to its
other types") as beneficial.

Tests (policies/tests/named_counter_targeting.rs): Omo's counter reads as
beneficial and a CantBlock-defined counter as harmful; anti_self_harm scores
the AI's own land above an opponent's for Omo's attack trigger; over 40 seeds
the Easy AI puts the counters on its own permanents (before: own 0,
opponents 79, none 1; after: own 79, opponents 0, none 1).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
